+## 3. Streams, environment, executable lookup and unattended operation
+
+- stdin: no verb reads it. `grep` for `input(`, `getpass`, `sys.stdin` and `isatty` over `src/patchtrace` finds nothing. Child processes get `stdin=DEVNULL` (`jobs.py:296`; Windows: `jobs.py:144`). There is no prompt on any path: every confirmation is a flag (`--consent-hosts`, `--consent-plan`, `--consent-providers`, `--consent-online`, `--confirm-material`, `--confirm-same-component`, `--accept-*`, `--user-attest-pair`, `--yes`, `--force`, `--overwrite`), and a missing flag is exit 2 with the exact plan or reason (section 8, item 10). A new verb adds no prompt (section 7).
+- stdout: UTF-8 with `errors=replace` (`cli.py:887-889`). With `--json` the only stdout content is the envelope (help excepted); in the inventory of 2026-11-11 (not committed) a probe of 109 invocations on a generated sample project, stdin closed, printed exactly one document per `--json` call and no traceback (synthetic; the probe list is not part of the test suite and was not re-run in full for this refresh).
+- stderr, in every mode: `request: <METHOD> <url>` before each network request (`cli.py:448, 552, 615, 624`; `intelligence/cli.py:226`); the exact plan before a consented fetch of `kb index sync`, `kb acquire` and `kev fetch` (`kbcorrelation/cli_online.py:1-16`; `kbcorrelation/cli_acquire.py:1-5`; `kev/cli.py:1-12`); progress (`cli.py:308`; `unified/cli.py:155-157`); `error: <message>` (`cli.py:897, 916`); `cancelled` (`cli.py:906`); extra validation findings (`intelligence/cli.py:139-146`); diagnostics (`cli_binexport.py:64-65`). A JSON consumer reads stdout only.
+- Untrusted text (advisory fields, file names, worker stderr, symbol names) is made terminal-safe before it is printed: `escape_text` in `cli._emit` (`cli.py:198-201`), `plain_text` (`intelligence/cli.py:103-108`; `cli.py:204-211`), `sanitize_text` (`unified/cli.py:140-143`).
+- Environment read: `PATCHTRACE_BINDIFF` (`cli_bindiff.py:19, 71`); `PATCHTRACE_CAPA`, `_FLOSS`, `_DIEC`, `_DIEC_DB`, `_DIEC_LIB`, `_CAPA_RULES`, `_CAPA_SIGS` (`intelligence/tools/cli.py:18-20`); `PATCHTRACE_BUNDLE_DIR` when locating the bundle (`backend_bundle.py:30, 126`); `PATCHTRACE_CHILD_ENV=inherit` to let an analysis child inherit the environment (`backend.py:248`); the variable named by `--api-key-env` (`cli.py:106, 190, 450`), never printed. Credentials are session-only: no verb stores a key. Analysis profiles come from the desktop profile directory (`enrichment.md` section 12).
