+### 7.2 Rules every verb of 7.1 follows
+
+1. Envelope and codes. Exactly one `enrichment-cli/1` document per `--json` call; exit codes 0, 2, 3, 4, 5 with the meanings of section 4; `command` is `verb action` on success and on failure (section 8, item 15 is a defect, not a model); a partial result exits 3; a missing or unopenable project directory, a bad argument, an inert flag and a missing consent each exit 2.
+2. No Qt. The verb is a `cli_commands/<verb>.py` adapter of at most 25 lines over a Qt-free `<package>/cli.py` (section 9); the headless entry never imports `PySide6` or `patchtrace.ui` (test, section 11).
+3. No prompt on any path. Consent and confirmation are flags; a network verb announces each request on stderr and needs an exact host or plan; a secret is never a flag value (name an environment variable instead).
+4. Read-only verbs never write to the project. They open it with `ProjectService.open(path, maintenance=False)` (`service.py:102-110`), take no write path at all, and say in their spec that they are read-only. (The built-in `cli._open` opens with maintenance on, which section 8, item 24 records.)
+5. Mutations go through `ProjectService` only. No verb edits `project.sqlite3`, a sidecar or a raw output directly; the spec of each mutating verb names the service method it calls, and a failed mutation preserves earlier committed results (`AGENTS.md`).
+6. Output files. A verb that writes a file writes only to a path the caller names, outside the project unless it goes through the service, and replaces an existing file only behind an explicit flag (section 8, item 14 records the spellings already in use).
+7. Determinism and bounds. Sorted iteration, no clock in results, every loop over untrusted input bounded; untrusted text escaped before printing (section 3).
+8. A help page per verb. `docs/help/NN-cli-<verb>.md`, whose first line is the verb's heading `# \`patchtrace <verb>\``, linked from `docs/help/README.md`; `tests/test_help_docs.py:54, 70-75` fail otherwise. The adapter and its help page land together.
+9. Parity statement. A GUI capability that the verb deliberately does not offer (an interactive viewer, a drag-and-drop gesture) is listed in the verb's spec under "not applicable" with the reason, so that "impossible or inappropriate" is a recorded decision and not an omission.
+10. Tests. Each verb adds a contract test of the shape in section 11 and states its evidence class; fixture tests are never live evidence.
