+Status: built. `src/patchtrace/cli_commands/` exists at `882d1ca0` with the registry (`__init__.py`, 89 lines), the shared helpers (`_support.py`) and 13 adapters. The rules below describe the code; where a test enforces one, the test is named.
+
+- A verb is `cli_commands/<verb>.py`: the file name with `_` read as `-` (`cli_commands/__init__.py:40-41`; `build_env.py` is `build-env`). The name matches `^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{1,23}$` (`:34`), is unique and is not in `cli.COMMANDS`; a file that names a built-in verb or that two files claim makes both unavailable, never an override (`:57-69`; `tests/test_cli_registry.py`, `test_a_built_in_verb_name_is_never_overridden`, `test_two_files_claiming_one_verb_are_both_unavailable`).
+- The adapter exports `COMMAND = CliCommand(name, summary, build, run)` (`:26-37`). `summary` is 1 to 80 printable ASCII characters; `build(sub)` adds and returns the full parser; `run(args, cancel)` returns 0, 2, 3, 4 or 5 and raises `CliError` for 2 and 3. The adapter re-exports `CliError`, `emit` (= `cli._emit`) and the exit constants (`:18-22`).
+- Adapters stay small. At most 25 lines (the 13 range from 17 to 23), importing only the package and the standard library at module level; the feature is imported inside `build` and `run`, so listing the verbs loads no feature (`tests/test_cli_registry.py:403-410, 459-463`; `tests/test_cli_commands_features.py:85-90`). The adapter wraps the feature's own Qt-free `<package>/cli.py`, which owns the grammar (`add_parser` and `run`, or `register` for a dispatcher that already exists). `kb` and `search` are passthrough adapters (`_support.py:7-14`).
+- Discovery is by file. `discover()` returns `(verbs, failed)`, both sorted; files that start with `_` are skipped (`:44-47, 57-69`). `names()` lists `cli.COMMANDS` then every discovered verb, unavailable ones included, importing nothing (`:72-74`; test: 25 ms budget with slack, `test_names_over_twenty_verbs_is_fast_and_imports_none_of_them`). `register_all(sub, invoked)` builds the full parser of the invoked verb only and a bare listing for the rest (`:77-89`). The parser's choices equal `names()` (`test_parser_choices_equal_names_even_with_broken_clashing_and_duplicate_files`).
+- A broken file is listed as unavailable and exits 3. It keeps its name in `patchtrace --help` with the summary `unavailable (could not be loaded)` (`:23, 88-89`); invoking it, with or without `--help`, exits 3 `PT-CLI-COMMAND` while the other verbs still run (`:85-86`; `tests/test_cli_registry.py:365`). One broken file never hides another (`:183`).
+- Labels. `register_all` sets `command_label` to the verb name (`:84`); the feature emits `verb action` on success. The failure label gap is section 8, item 15.
+- Seam budget. `cli.py` may exceed 914 lines by 6 and holds exactly one function-level `cli_commands` import (`cli.py:183-184`; it is at 920 lines now); `cli.COMMANDS` stays the 11 built-in verbs; the registry module stays at most 90 lines (`tests/test_cli_registry.py:394-401`). A new verb edits none of `cli.py`, `tools/frozen_smoke.py` or `tests/test_acceptance_smoke.py` and adds no PyInstaller hook: the smoke list is derived from the registry (`test_the_frozen_smoke_list_is_derived_from_the_registry`) and the hook collects the whole package (`test_the_hook_collects_exactly_the_registry_package_and_its_files`).
+- Qt-free. The registry and discovery import neither Qt nor pydantic (`test_the_registry_and_discovery_never_import_qt_or_pydantic`); a feature dispatcher may import pydantic once its verb is invoked (`pilot/cli.py:1-12`).
